7,18,0.721,0.543,[[1,1]],[["94f24a4f_594e5533",6,0,1,"I think it's OK to keep this enum value (maybe renaming it to something like `kTextOrImage` makes sense) in a later CL so its usage is clearer, but for this CL we should at least have a comment…"],["d972e3d3_de5ffce0",6,0,1,"Would it make sense to rename this enum to `IMAGE`?"]],0,7],[7208621,20419,19,0.198,0.14,[[17,0]],[],0,8],[7122761,20425,329,7.579,6.176,[[6,0.994,4,328],[11,0.006,2,1]],[["ca04e254_ab0d626c",36,-26,1,"```suggestion static DevToolsPolicyDialog* Create(content::WebContents* web_contents); ```"],["bb8bfee1_37cdb651",2,-23,1,"How exactly? Can you add screenshots of before and after?"],["16d4c001_48426efa",37,-2,1,"So which one is the delegate here? The outer class also implements `views::DialogDelegate`. What purpose does the inner class serve? Does the outer class need to implement `views::DialogDelegate`?"],["85b24edc_fe8ba293",37,-2,1,"This logic seems brittle: 1) You create a raw pointer dialog_manager. 2) You pass ownership to PolicyDialogDelegate via WrapUnique. 3) You store the raw pointer in a static map. 4) You use…"],["9e6cbaf3_bb17dd2d",38,-2,1,"nit: This check is not needed"],["9f58b5bd_65ea4de5",37,-2,1,"Why is this needed?"],["cb00e353_db8efc99",37,-2,1,"Isn't this redundant given the line 105?"],["efba6c61_d91e89fa",36,-1,1,"This could be private now."],["f5273e28_82be71b3",37,-1,1,"If the WebContents is destroyed (e.g., the user closes the tab), the modal dialog is forcibly closed during the teardown sequence. Depending on the exact timing of the destruction phases,…"],["2f9ee3fd_efa016fc",38,0,1,"Using base::Seconds(1) renders the test flaky on slow bots and unnecessarily slow on fast ones. It does not guarantee the cleanup has happened. Since you have a TestObserver, add a method…"]],0,9],[7228582,20427,92,2.344,1.853,[[18,0.874,0,81],[14,0.126,2,11]],[["2139ac12_8a565793",39,-1,0,"Having two different disabling functions feels redundant and unclear as to what the source of truth is. I’m trying to mentally work out how the current code doesn’t work, and I admit that I’m…"],["a4531685_9ca5c0fe",40,-1,1,"I think a different level or just removing this log would be more appropriate, I don't think reaching this line really indicates an error right?"],["aacc0571_f9486db7",2,-1,1,"Link a bug. It can just be crbug.com/442892562 since this CL is a continuation of the work you're doing for it."],["f5d14be2_e3696e16",25,-1,1,"```suggestion profile(), browser_->tab_strip_model()->GetActiveWebContents())); ```"]],0,10],[7205188,20431,74,2.202,1.731,[[19,0.616,0,47],[1,0.384,2,27]],[["38086477_e35be7bf",41,-8,0,"Is it difficult to split the source in two? It doesn't seem like this enum is used that many places and if we can explicitly say \"this is an image\" or \"this is text\", it removes any risk of future…"],["07e2490d_d4a3af6d",42,-4,1,"Typo in double comment :D"],["2521ae3d_0e25c904",43,-4,1,"The problem with this function is that several formats are not covered (ex. svg, gif, webp, bmp). Instead of this, how about we add a `data_source` argument so caller code can simply choose the type…"],["dd45a6b5_1beafc00",42,-4,1,"Why do we need this comment?"],["e56ee65d_cbb330ca",41,-4,1,"Why it this exposed as a global function and do we expect to you use it anywhere else? If yes, I would suggest moving it to some file with common utilities, otherwise it can be in unnamed namespace…"],["f1199053_e54fbf7c",43,-4,1,"It could be useful to add some comment in the header file to explain this behavior."],["34b194d9_0b902e19",44,-1,1,"nit: why not just initialize the string with `\\x89PNG\\r\\n\\x1a\\n`?"],["56d28e2c_2045f919",42,-1,1,"Nit: while accurate, we don't need this comment anymore. It was previously justifying the use of `kImageContentType` when `data_source_` was `STRING`. But this code doesn't need any justification!"],["88076ddd_0e2f7e20",5,-1,1,"nit: using enterprise_connectors::ConnectorUploadRequest"],["9c648709_af1de133",45,-1,1,"nit: please add a comment explaining why this parameter is needed"]],0,11]]}